Feature: The home page is the page that was approved

  A woman hears about Emi from somebody and opens myemi.app. She has never seen the product, and
  this one page is everything she has to go on before she is asked for 29.99 pounds a month.

  The page she has been reading until now follows a prose brief. It says Emi is a calm journal and
  that only she can read her days, and then it asks for the money. The board the operator approved
  says six more things, and each of them is the product deciding what it is: that a forecast is a
  range of days and how sure Emi is, that the education is accurate and plain about what people are
  taught not to ask, that the community is a place to ask and to help, that one person is building
  this and these are his reasons, that her data is encrypted, and what a month costs and the three
  ways to pay it.

  One band of the board is not on the page. It says what other people think of Emi, and the board
  draws six cards of it as holes in brackets, because nobody had written a review when it was drawn.
  Nobody has since, so the page holds that band back whole and draws eight of the nine.

  So the page becomes the board. A browser reads the two side by side and refuses a difference of
  more than one pixel in a thousand, which is the scenario in the browser suite under this same
  sentence. What a picture cannot see is read here instead, because each of these is worth about
  two hundred pixels on a page of seven million and would pass that comparison on its own: a band
  that draws a rule on four sides where the board draws one, a link in the legal line that lost its
  underline, and the arithmetic of the ring, which only answers once a hand moves the slider.

  Scenario: the home page matches the approved design pixel for pixel
    Given a woman opens the home page of myemi.app
    Then she reads eight of the nine bands of the approved board, in the board's order and on its grounds
    And every sentence of the board is on the page, in English, in Russian and in Spanish
    And the brand line stands over the hero in capitals, and is still the one line nobody translates
    And the ring starts at day 8 in the follicular phase, and answers every other day the way the board does
    And every rule sits on the sides the board puts it on, and on no others
    And the five links of the legal line are underlined, because the board underlines them
    And the page writes no style of its own, so her browser refuses nothing
    And a browser holds the page against the design at every width, and keeps the picture of any difference
